spans.s:
व्यं॑स a. having the shoulders apart, i.e.
broad-shouldered;
 m. N. of a demon.

व्य॑क्त a. adorned, fair, manifest, clear, n. adv.;
 abstr.
˚ता f.

व्यङ्ग्य a. clear, distinct;
 implicit ((rh.)), abstr. ˚ता
f., ˚त्व n.

व्यञ्जक a. manifesting, betraying (gen. or —˚);
 abstr.
˚त्व n.

व्यतिकर m. mixing, confusing;
 contact, union;
confusion, disaster, accident.

व्यतिक्रम m. passing, getting a start;
 transgression,
violation, disregard, omission, also = seq.

व्यतिरिक्त a. reaching beyond (acc.), excessive,
abundant;
 richer or superior in (instr. or —˚), increased by (—˚);
haughty, arrogant.

व्यथन a. exciting, disturbing;
 n. wavering, agitation,
uneasiness.

व्यधिकरण a. relating to another subject;
 n.
incongruency (g.).

व्यध्व m. half the way;
 loc. व्यध्वे॑ or व्य॑ध्वे
adv. midway.

व्यपदेश m. designation, appellation, name, esp.
family-name;
 pretext, pretence.

व्यपदेशिन् a. = prec.;
 —˚ designating, appealing or
conforming one's self to.

व्यपाश्रय m. seat, place, refuge, support;
 adj. —˚
resorting to, trusting in.

व्यपेक्षा f. regard, consideration;
 expectation,
supposition.

व्यभिचार m. going asunder or astray, failure;
offence, going beyond, transgressing, sin, crime, esp. adultery (of a
wife).

व्यभिचारिन् a. going asunder or astray, infidel,
adulterous;
 going beyond, transgressing (—˚).

व्यर्थ a. useless, vain (n. adv.);
 unmeaning,
contradictory;
 destitute of wealth or money, i.g. destitute of (instr.).

व्यलीक a. false, deceitful;
 n. adv., as subst. falsehood,
untruth, deceit, offence, pain, grief.

व्यवधान n. lying or stepping between, intercession,
mediation, separation, distinction, interruption;
 also = seq.

व्यवस्था f. distinctness, particularity;
 constancy,
stability;
 state, position;
 decision, rule.

व्यवस्थित a. being in a state or position, situated,
standing or being in, resting or dependent on, sticking to (loc. or
—˚);
 settled, fixed, limited, constant;
 existing, appearing as (nom.,
instr., ger., adv., or —˚).

व्यवहर्तव्य a. to be used or employed;
 to be acted
or proceeded (n. impers.).

व्यवहर्तृ a. occupied or dealing with (instr.);
 m.
judge.

व्यवहार m. procedure, conduct, way of acting;
intercourse with (सह);
 usage, custom, activity, occupation, dealing
with or in (loc. or —˚);
 business, commerce, trade;
 legal dispute,
lawsuit, litigation, contract, stipulation, administration of justice.

व्यवहारवन्त् a. dealing in (—˚);
 m. man of
business.

व्यवहारिन् a. proceeding with, dealing in (—˚);
 m. man
of business, merchant.

व्यसन n. moving hither and thither, activity, industry,
propensity or devotion to, zeal for (loc. or —˚);
 passion, whim, hobby,
evil habit, vice;
 ill luck, adversity, calamity.

व्यसनिन् a. active, exerting one's self;
 intently
attached to, fond of (loc. or —˚);
 having evil passions, vicious,
wicked;
 unlucky, unfortunate. Abstr. ˚निता f., ˚त्व n.

व्यस्त a. torn asunder, shaken, tossed;
 divided, separated;
separate, single, several, various;
 व्यस्ते काले sometimes, now and
then.

व्या व्य॑यति व्य॑य˚ते pp. वीत॑ (q.v.) wrap, veil,
envelop;
 M. refl. — अप unveil, uncover;
 M. extricate one's self i.e.
deny. अपि cover. आ wrap round (acc.), hide one's self in (loc.).
उप hang about (esp. the sacred cord over the left shoulder). नि
wind or hang about. परि wrap around;
 M. wind something as cover round
one's self. सम् A. roll up, envelop;
 veil in (instr.), M. refl. — Cf.
उ॑पवीत, नि॑वीत, प॑रिवीत, संवीत.

व्याकरण n. putting asunder, separation^1;
 explanation,
manifestation;
 analysis, grammar.
[1] Correction submitted by AnnaRybakovaT, Jim Funderburk. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/25.

व्याकुल a. thoroughly filled with or full of (instr. or
—˚);
 quite intent upon or occupied with (—˚);
 confused, disarranged,
perplexed, bewildered. Abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

व्याकुलय् व्याकुल˚यति confuse, disarrange;
 pp.
व्याकुलित = prec.

व्याघात m. stroke, blow, shot;
 agitation, confusion;
shock, defeat;
 obstacle, hindrance.

व्याघ्र॑ m. tiger, first or best of (—˚);
 f. व्याघ्री
tigress. — Abstr. ˚ता† f., ˚त्व† n.

व्याज m. (n.) deceit, fraud, false semblance, pretext,
pretence;
 ˚— & instr. adv.;
 adj. —˚ having the mere semblance of, only
appearing as.

व्या॑त्त a. torn asunder, opened;
 n. the opened mouth, the
jaws.

व्यापिन् a. spreading, extending;
 reaching through, filling,
containing (—˚).

व्या॑प्ति f. obtaining, reaching, penetrating, filling,
containing;
 universal pervasion, general rule.

व्यायत a. torn asunder, stretched out, long;
 strong,
vigorous, abstr. ˚त्व n.

व्यायाम॑ m. exertion, bodily exercise, struggle, fight;
 a
fathom (cf. व्याम॑).

व्यावर्तक f. ˚र्तिका excluding, removing;
 abstr.
˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

व्यावहारिक f. ई relating to practice or business;
common, real (opp. ideal);
 judicial;
 n. intercourse, commerce, settled
usage or law.

व्या॑वृत्त a. turned away (lit. & fig.), liberated from or
rid of (abl. or —˚);
 opened, divided, different from, incompatible with
(—˚);
 ceased, perished, at an end.

व्या॑वृत्ति f. turning away, getting rid or being deprived
of (abl.);
 exclusion, removal;
 separation, distinction, difference;
conclusion, end.

व्यास m. separation, division;
 extension, diffusion,
prolixity;
 N. of a celebrated Ṛṣi and author.

व्याहार m. utterance, talk, conversation;
 singing (of
birds).

व्याहारिन् a. talking, speaking, singing;
 resounding with
(—˚).

व्या॑हृत a. uttered, spoken, communicated;
 n. talk,
speech, singing (of birds).
